<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ikaria</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Icaria</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ikaria is a Greek island in the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a>, west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samo">Samos</a>, named in legend after Icarus, who fell into the sea nearby. Under Ottoman rule from the 16th century, it expelled the Turkish garrison in July 1912 and was briefly the Free State of Icaria before uniting with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> in November 1912. Its people are noted for their long life expectancy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ikaria.jpg" alt="Ikaria" width="320" height="156" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sentinel-2 cloudless 2016 by EOX IT Services GmbH is licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International ... · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ikaria_by_Sentinel-2_Cloudless.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
